      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you could get the same effect with less code:\n\n        if (mag \u003e 16777216.0) { // 2^24, when f32 loses 1px precision\n            // This brings the components of a and b to be within [-1, 1] before the vector\u0027s length\n            // is calculated inside the normalize() call.\n            float invMag \u003d 1.0 / mag;\n            a *\u003d invMag;\n            b *\u003d invMag;\n        }\n        return normalize(a - b);\n        \nIt might also be faster (and, if we\u0027re lucky, accurate enough) to just always scale down. Branches are expensive; reciprocals are cheap; multiplies are very very cheap. WDYT about this version?\n\n        float invMag \u003d 1.0 / mag;\n        a *\u003d invMag;\n        b *\u003d invMag;\n        return normalize(a - b);",
